      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the 200 mg/day maximum. Nothing you've told me gives a clinical reason for it, and I can't treat it as intentional.\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** You've said you work in finance. A non-clinician can't confirm a dose, so your confirmation doesn't replace a prescriber's review.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Contact the treating prescriber and ask them to confirm or correct the dose. If the intended dose is within range, such as 100 mg once daily, I can enter it once they give me the number.\n- If the prescriber really does want a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves and talk with pharmacy first.\n- If you think a dose like this has already been given or ordered somewhere else, tell the charge nurse or pharmacy right away."
      }
